      "description": "Transcribe audio to MIDI\n\nTranscribes one of the signed-in suno.com user's own finished songs into a\nmulti-track MIDI file, as suno.com's Studio does. Any song in their library\nworks, including a stem. Requires the `audio.midi` feature (otherwise `403`\n`feature_not_on_plan`), a token that grants `library:read` and\n`credits:spend`, and a suno.com plan with Studio (Premier; otherwise `403`\nwith reason `plan_required`). An API key gets 403.\n\nThe first call starts the transcription and answers `processing`; call\nagain with the same id until `status` is `ok`, usually within a minute.\nA transcription\ncosts 10 of the user's suno.com credits (none for a stem from suno.com's generative Get Stems), charged once when it finishes; a\nsong already transcribed, here or in Studio, is served again for free.\nTell the user the cost before the first call.\n\nOn `ok`, `url` downloads the `.mid` file under the song's title, and\n`instruments` lists its tracks with how many notes each has. Hosts that\nshow apps render a download button for `url`; elsewhere, share it.\n`failed` means the transcription errored and nothing was charged.\n\nRefusals carry a `reason`: `plan_required` (403, `feature_not_on_plan`),\n`quota_exhausted` (402, `insufficient_credits`), `invalid_asset` (404,\n`not_found`, a song that failed to generate) and `not_ready` (422,\n`not_ready`, a song still generating; call again once it has finished).",
