      "description": "Publish, unpublish, or allow or stop remixing of a song\n\nChanges the settings on one of the signed-in suno.com user's songs, as the\ncontrols on its suno.com page do. Send `visibility`, `can_remix` or both;\nanything omitted is left as it is.\n\n- `visibility: public` publishes the song: anyone can find it on the user's\n  profile and in search. It is never entered in a remix contest. A song\n  already streaming is held and published when it finishes, answering\n  `publish_pending: true` with `visibility` still `private`; one not yet\n  streaming is a retryable 409, so wait a moment or use `audio-wait`. A song\n  suno.com won't let its owner publish, such as one with vocals from a\n  source they can't publish, is a 403. Only publishes that succeed count\n  toward 100 in a UTC day; past that, one more is a 429 `quota_exceeded`\n  that changes nothing. `private` unpublishes it, withdraws it from any open\n  remix contest, and is never capped.\n- `can_remix: false` stops other users from covering, extending or mashing\n  up the song; the user's own remixes are unaffected. More than 20 changes a\n  minute is a 429. Refused with 403: a contest entry (its remix setting\n  belongs to the contest), opening a remix of registered-catalog music to\n  further remixing, and an account outside suno.com's remix feature. The\n  error names which.\n\n`can_remix` is applied first. If it succeeds and `visibility` then fails,\nthe error says `can_remix` was changed. Only the song's owner can change\nits settings. Only for a suno.com user whose token grants `library:write`;\nan API key gets 403.",
