      "description": "Start uploading a MIDI file\n\nStarts uploading a MIDI file (.mid or .midi, up to 256 KB) a song can play\nfrom: pass the finished upload's `midi_upload_id` to `POST /v0/audio`. Call\nit as soon as the user wants a song from their own MIDI, before they attach\nanything, so the uploader is where they drop the file.\n\nWhen the user attached a MIDI file in this chat, pass it as `file`: it is\nuploaded and checked at once, and the response is the finished upload, as\nfrom midi-upload-complete, with nothing left to send.\n\nOtherwise POST the file to `upload_url` as `multipart/form-data` within 10\nminutes, every `upload_fields` entry first and the file last as `file`, for\nexample `curl -F 'key=…' -F 'policy=…' … -F 'file=@score.mid' '<upload_url>'`,\nand call midi-upload-complete. If you can't send the file yourself, the\nuploader shown with this call lets the user pick it; when it reports the\nupload, carry on with what the user asked for without asking again.\n`upload_url` and its fields are credentials for this one upload. Only for a\nuser signed in with Suno; an API key gets 403.",
