      "description": "Make keyframes or clips for several shots at once\n\nStarts one generation for each of up to 8 shots of a Sequence in one call,\neach landing in its shot as image-create and video-create do with a\n`shot_id`. `step: keyframes` makes each shot's opening image from its `prompt`;\n`step: clips` makes each shot's video from its `prompt`, opening on the shot's\nkeyframe (or `first_frame_asset_id`; with neither, from the prompt alone), covering\nthe shot, made for the Sequence's song. For one continuous take across shots,\n`continues_shot_id` extends a neighbour's clip from where it's cut and\n`leads_into_shot_id` ends on a neighbour's first frame, or on its keyframe before\nit holds a clip; both bridge the two.\n`aspect` defaults to the\nSequence's. Answers at once with each shot's `status`: `started` with its\n`generation_id` and its takes' `labels` (call visuals-wait with all of them), `rate_limited` (wait\n`retry_after_seconds`, then send those shots again), `moderation_limited` (moderation\nblocked too many recent videos: stop and tell the user, don't retry), `refused` with\nthe reason, and for a moderation refusal its `moderation_reason` and what to do in\n`error` (revise at most once, only for a named artist, character or person; never\nreword past moderation), or `unknown` (it may have started: retry only with the same `idempotency_key`).\nA started shot with an `error` started but isn't in its shot yet. Creates are\nlimited to about 10 a minute. Spends the user's Visuals credits like the\nsingle tools: before a large batch, send it first with `dry_run: true`, which\nstarts nothing and answers with its exact cost, and tell the user.\nSend an `idempotency_key` and reuse it when retrying, so a retry\nreplays the shots that started instead of paying twice. Only for a suno.com\nuser whose token grants `visuals`; anyone else gets 404.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "aspect": {
            "description": "The shape; the Sequence's when absent.",
            "enum": [
              "1:1",
              "9:16",
              "16:9"
            ],
            "type": "string"
          },
          "dry_run": {
            "description": "True prices every shot of this exact batch in Visuals credits and answers with a quote, starting nothing and spending nothing. Only a real call checks the model's aspects, prompt length and inputs, so it can still refuse a quoted shot.",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "id": {
            "description": "The `sequence_id`.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "idempotency_key": {
            "description": "Opaque key for safely retrying a creation request. Keys contain 1–255 bytes,\nare scoped to the authenticated account across all supported creation\noperations, and are retained for at least 24 hours. Repeating the same key\nwith the same operation and parameters returns the original resource and sets\n`Idempotency-Replayed: true`; reusing it with different input returns `409`.\nA replay never re-emits webhooks. Audio replays return the current clip\nstatus from a live read.\n",
            "maxLength": 255,
            "minLength": 1,
            "pattern": "\\S",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "model": {
            "description": "An image model for keyframes or a video model for clips, from visuals-models; image-4 for keyframes and the task's default for clips when absent. A clip for a shot citing characters or a set with no keyframe is reference_to_video, refused unless you name a model that serves it, so make the shot's keyframe first.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "resolution": {
            "description": "For clips, one of the model's `resolutions` from visuals-models; its default when absent.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "shots": {
            "items": {
              "properties": {
                "continues_shot_id": {
                  "description": "For clips, the shot right before this one in the cut, whose clip this one extends, picking up on the frame where that clip is cut, so the two play as one take. That shot must already hold a clip, not one made in this call. Not with `first_frame_asset_id`. This shot's characters and set go along as references on video-1, video-2 and video-5 with no `last_frame_asset_id`; otherwise the clip keeps only the people already in that shot's frame, and the shot's `note` says so.",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "first_frame_asset_id": {
                  "description": "For clips, the image the clip opens on, or a preset's `ref`; the shot's keyframe when absent.",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "last_frame_asset_id": {
                  "description": "For clips, an image for the clip to end on.",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "leads_into_shot_id": {
                  "description": "For clips, the shot right after this one in the cut, whose clip this one ends on the first frame of, so it runs into that shot. Before that shot holds a clip, or when this call makes one opening on its keyframe, this one ends on that keyframe, so joined shots can all be made in one call. While that shot's clip is being made in an earlier call, wait for it. Send it only where the user wants the two shots to play as one take, since shots cut by default; this one needs a keyframe, `first_frame_asset_id` or `continues_shot_id` to open on. With `continues_shot_id` too, the clip bridges the two and plays whole, so the shot must run a whole number of seconds, 5 to 15. Not with `last_frame_asset_id`.",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "lip_sync": {
                  "description": "For clips, false asks that no one on screen sing or mouth the words. Needs a Sequence with a song.",
                  "type": "boolean"
                },
                "prompt": {
                  "description": "For a keyframe, the image (with the style, naming the shot's characters and set); for a clip, what happens and how the camera moves.",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "shot_id": {
                  "description": "A shot of the Sequence, at most once per call.",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "shot_id",
                "prompt"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            },
            "maxItems": 8,
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array"
          },
          "step": {
            "description": "`keyframes`: each shot's opening image. `clips`: each shot's video.",
            "enum": [
              "keyframes",
              "clips"
            ],
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "id",
          "step",
          "shots"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
