      "description": "Assemble a music video\n\nCuts ready video clips, and stills held for their `duration_s`, end to end, in\norder, over a song and renders the result to an MP4 with the song as its\nsoundtrack, from `song_start_s` until the clips or the song run out. Stills\nalone make a free animatic. For a cut planned shot by shot, use\nsequence-create instead. `trim_start_s` and `trim_end_s` trim a clip on its own clock. With\n`lyrics: true` the song's words are burned in as they are sung. Answers at once\nwith the render's `id`; call visuals-wait with it (a render takes a few\nminutes), then visuals-download. Rendering is free. A clip still being made is\na 400: wait for it first. Send an `idempotency_key` and reuse it when retrying\nafter an error, so a retry finishes the same video instead of starting another;\na new cut takes a new key. Only for a suno.com user whose token grants\n`visuals`; anyone else gets 404.",
